//? Title: PWC-Net: shared pyramids and visible tensor flow fitting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Two observed frames must identify motion despite weak texture and occlusion. PWC-Net narrows the search through shared pyramids,backward feature warping and local cost volumes. Hand correlations,warp units and dilated context precede full/compact graph checks,published Middlebury pairs,explicit SGD/Adam and immutable pair-only deployment,with every held-out motion error reported.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/pwcnet.cpp`.

> The method

At each coarse-to-fine level,a shared feature extractor represents both
frames. Current flow warps the second features before a radius4 correlation
volume measures local matches. Dense estimators predict fixed input-pixel/20
flow;learned upflow/upfeature connect levels,and a dilated residual context
refines the finest field. Only observed RGB enters forward inference.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/pwcnet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/pwcnet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/pwcnet_concept.tikz > build/pwcnet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/pwcnet_concept.svg build/pwcnet_concept.dvi > build/pwcnet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
