> Dilated context adds reach without inventing learned taps

After dense estimation at level2,a seven-layer context residual uses dilation
rates1,2,4,8,16,1,1. Portable tensor expansion inserts zeros between the nine
learned3x3 taps;it retains a differentiable mapping to every original tap.
Dilation2 gives a5x5 effective kernel,and dilation4 gives9x9,each with nine
learned locations. Native signed-convolution oracles cover all values and
input/kernel derivatives through rates1,2,4,8 and16.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pwcnet_context.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  const auto kernel = n::ones({3, 3, 1, 1}).requires_grad_();
  const auto two = n::expand_dilated_kernel(kernel, 2),
             four = n::expand_dilated_kernel(kernel, 4);
  const auto gradient = n::grad(n::sum(two) + n::sum(four), {kernel})[0];
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(two.reshape({5, 5}), {0}), 0, 1),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(four.reshape({9, 9}), {0}), 0, 1);
  a.title("Dilation2:effective5x5").x_label("kernel column").y_label("kernel row");
  b.title("Dilation4:effective9x9").x_label("kernel column").y_label("kernel row");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg("build/pwcnet_context.svg");
  std::print("Nine learned taps in each expansion;gradient of summed two expansions is2 at "
             "all nine taps,max error {:.3g}.\n",
             n::max(n::abs(gradient - 2.)).item());
}
```
