> Actual published pairs and an explicit SGD reference

Use the same reproducible Middlebury preparation as FlowNetS. Place the
official frame-pair and GT ZIP files in `build/cnn-datasets/optical_flow`,then
run from the repository root:

```{cpp, flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("optical_flow", (cache / "optical_flow").string());
}
```
// result_begin:
// result_end

The pinned frame/GT SHA256 values are
`dc7afbab15a7da40b52d633f825191bf693e227320bb624546ed9f2f8d668e50` and
`e967b729cc47a493b3226515e0172224e503f7b14a54f97660f8d5f745632ab9`.
Raw little-endian flow ingress and tensor finite/abs<1e9 validity preserve
published ground truth. Original RGB is divided by255;neither images nor
flow are resized. A predetermined5x5 tensor origin grid selects the first
eight unique64px crops per scene with>409 valid samples. The manifest retains
all scene IDs,families,dimensions and crop coordinates. This is a fresh
custom subset,not the old external archive or official evaluation.

Fit:Dimetrodon,Grove2,Grove3,Hydrangea(32 crops,three families).
Validation:RubberWhale(eight crops,one family).
Test:Urban2,Urban3,Venus(24 crops,two families). Related Grove and Urban
scenes stay together. Crops overlap within a scene,so test represents three
source pairs. The source data include photographed and rendered imagery.

Fit the two-coordinate constant reference with one visible SGD(.5) step on
summed masked-coordinate MSE. An independent tensor mean checks its result.
This baseline is fitted only on training families;zero flow has no parameters.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pwcnet_prior.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";

  std::filesystem::path root = cache / "optical_flow";
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_FLOW_DIR"))
    root = p;
  else
    dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("optical_flow", root.string());
  const auto split = m::LoadFlowPairs(root);

  n::ParameterStore constant(173, n::DType::Float64);
  const auto q = constant.get("flow", {2}, n::init::zeros());
  n::OptimizerConfig opt;
  opt.kind = n::OptimizerKind::Sgd;
  n::Optimizer sgd(constant, .5, opt);
  const auto target = split.fit.flow.to(n::DType::Float64),
             mask = split.fit.valid.to(n::DType::Float64);
  for (int step = 0; step < 1; ++step) {
    const auto loss = n::sum(
        n::sum(mask * n::square(q.reshape({1, 1, 1, 2}) - target), {0, 1, 2}) / n::sum(mask));
    sgd.minimize(loss);
  }
  const auto fitted = q.detach().to(n::DType::Float32);
  const auto closed = m::FitMeanFlow(split.fit);
  const auto expected =
      n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{closed[0], closed[1]}, {2}).to(n::DType::Float32);
  const double parity = n::max(n::abs(fitted - expected)).item();
  if (parity > 1e-8)
    return 1;
  const auto first = m::FlowBatch(split.fit, {0, 8, 16, 24});
  const auto reference = n::ones(first.flow.shape()) * fitted.reshape({1, 1, 1, 2});
  const auto warped = m::FlowWarp(first.second, reference).value;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  n::save_npz("build/pwcnet_prior.npz", {{"flow", fitted}});
  n::save_image_grid(m::FlowPreviewTiles(first, reference, warped),
                     "figures/pwcnet_inputs.png", 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 2);
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.bars({0., 1.}, fitted.to_vector<double>(), "SGD-fitted mean", {147, 51, 234})
      .title("Visible SGD fits constant input-pixel flow")
      .x_label("0 horizontal,1 vertical")
      .y_label("input-image pixels")
      .y_limits(-1.1, .35)
      .size(950, 480);
  plot.save_svg("build/pwcnet_prior.svg");
  std::print("One SGD(.5) update;mean oracle parity {:.3g};dx/dy {:.6f}/{:.6f}px.\n| split | "
             "crops | scenes | related families | GT pixels |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n",
             parity, fitted.to_vector<double>()[0], fitted.to_vector<double>()[1]);
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::string, m::FlowData>> splits = {
      {"fit", split.fit}, {"validation", split.validation}, {"test", split.test}};
  for (const auto &item : splits) {
    const auto scenes = item.second.scene_ids.to_vector<int>(),
               families = item.second.family_ids.to_vector<int>();
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", item.first, item.second.first.size(0),
               std::set<int>(scenes.begin(), scenes.end()).size(),
               std::set<int>(families.begin(), families.end()).size(),
               n::count_nonzero(item.second.valid).item<std::int64_t>());
  }
}
```
