\image(figures/pwcnet_training.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Forty-eight visible complete-model Adam updates supervise every pyramid head. Validation selects the checkpoint independently of test metrics;there is no hidden fitting method or pretrained state.)
\alttext(Forty-eight visible complete-model Adam updates supervise every pyramid head. Validation selects the checkpoint independently of test metrics;there is no hidden fitting method or pretrained state.)


\image(figures/pwcnet_metrics.svg)
\caption(Every held-out crop contributes to equal-image-weighted endpoint error. Initial,zero and SGD-constant references accompany the selected PWC-Net. The second panel separates Urban2,Urban3 and Venus source pairs.)
\alttext(Held-out PWC-Net endpoint errors and simple references,plus per-source-pair errors.)

\image(figures/pwcnet_predictions.png)
\caption(All24 held-out crops,two six-panel tiles per row. Each tile is first frame,second frame,published GT HSV,predicted HSV,EPE/5 red,and backward-warped second frame. Order:eight Urban2,eight Urban3,eight Venus. Display clipping never modifies numeric flow scores.)
\alttext(Observed published optical-flow image pairs with learned motion,color targets,errors and reconstructed warps.)

The selected epoch1 model reaches test EPE3.946422px,below its initial
4.370310 and the fitted constant’s4.174930,but above zero flow’s3.916913.
Its bad3 fraction .700714 is slightly below zero’s .701772,while the
constant has a lower .650614. Different aggregate metrics favor different
references;this short run does not establish a broad motion-quality gain.
Urban2/Urban3/Venus EPE2.412559/4.198488/5.228220px shows source variation.

Pyramid sharing,warp/cost geometry and complete gradients establish the
mechanism;they do not establish useful motion quality after a short fit.
No pretrained weights,FlyingChairs training,online augmentation or official
benchmark claim is made. Actual errors and zero/constant references keep
the source-family transfer limits visible.

> Conclusion

Tensor cost-volume derivatives,correct per-level warp units and portable dilated context establish the local mechanisms. Full connectivity and shared-gradient checks precede visible multiscale fitting on published targets. Independent pair-only restoration is immutable;actual field/warp errors and simple references delimit this short custom experiment.

> References

- [Sun et al.(2018),PWC-Net:CNNs for Optical Flow Using Pyramid,Warping,and Cost Volume](https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.02371).
- [Author PWC-Net graph](https://github.com/NVlabs/PWC-Net/blob/master/PyTorch/models/PWCNet.py).
- [Middlebury public optical-flow data](https://vision.middlebury.edu/flow/data/).
- [Baker et al.(2011),A Database and Evaluation Methodology for Optical Flow](https://vision.middlebury.edu/flow/floweval-ijcv2011.pdf).
